# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is git-ignored; never commit real values.
# See docs/security/MCL-34-family-access.md.

# Required. The shared family access code checked server-side at sign-in.
# Without it the gate fails closed: nobody can sign in and no submission is accepted.
AVALORIA_FAMILY_ACCESS_CODE=change-me-to-a-long-random-family-code

# Required for the protected admin inbox (MCL-50). A DIFFERENT value from the family
# access code above - that one is what the children hold in order to submit, so reusing
# it would let any child read every sibling's answers. Unset or blank, the admin inbox
# fails closed: /api/admin/inbox/submissions answers 503 and shows nothing. The child
# site is unaffected either way.
#
# This MUST differ from AVALORIA_FAMILY_ACCESS_CODE, and the difference is enforced
# rather than trusted: both gates share AVALORIA_SESSION_SECRET and the same signing
# construction, so identical codes make a child's session token and an adult's
# interchangeable. Set them equal (ignoring surrounding whitespace) and the whole admin
# surface fails closed - both /api/admin/session and the inbox read answer 503, and the
# server logs that the two codes must differ. The child site keeps working.
AVALORIA_ADMIN_ACCESS_CODE=change-me-to-a-long-random-admin-code

# Optional. Extra signing material for the session cookie, mixed in alongside the access
# code rather than instead of it. Changing either value invalidates existing sessions.
# Shared by the family and admin gates on purpose: it is signing material, not an
# identity, and the identity is already separated by the two access codes above.
# AVALORIA_SESSION_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Optional. Where the append-only JSONL inbox is written.
# AVALORIA_INBOX_DIR=.data/inbox

# Optional. Where unchanged original recordings are written (MCL-49).
#
# On the VPS this MUST point at a persistent volume or bind mount, not at a path inside
# the container's writable layer - a Coolify redeploy replaces that layer and would take
# every recording with it. Production uses the bind mount /opt/mc-legends/data/media,
# which the container sees as /data/media.
#
# Deliberately separate from AVALORIA_INBOX_DIR: that directory holds MCL-48's small
# JSONL rollback artefact, this one holds megabytes with a different backup sizing and a
# different retention question. Nothing serves this directory over HTTP - playback goes
# through the authorized admin route.
# AVALORIA_MEDIA_DIR=.data/media

# Optional. The largest audio upload accepted, in bytes. Default 8388608 (8 MiB),
# decided 2026-08-21.
#
# This number lives in three places that have to agree: here, the reverse proxy in front
# of the app (nginx `client_max_body_size`, which must be HIGHER to allow for multipart
# overhead - 12M is what production sets), and a CHECK constraint in migration 0002.
# Lowering it here needs no migration; raising it past the database's ceiling will be
# refused by that constraint, which is the intended order.
#
# Note for anyone changing the proxy: nginx's default is 1 MiB, so a vhost that simply
# omits client_max_body_size rejects almost every recording before the app ever sees it.
# AVALORIA_AUDIO_MAX_BYTES=8388608

# Optional. PostgreSQL connection for the durable inbox (MCL-48). Left unset, the
# file-based store above is used - which is also the rollback path if the database has
# to be taken out of the picture. Production connects over a Unix socket, so no password
# crosses a network and none belongs in this file:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://mcl_app:PASSWORD@/mcl?host=/var/run/postgresql

# Optional. Process-local MVP rate limits - see docs/security/MCL-34-family-access.md
# for what they do and do not protect.
# AVALORIA_SESSION_RATE_LIMIT=20
# AVALORIA_SESSION_RATE_WINDOW_MS=60000
# AVALORIA_INBOX_RATE_LIMIT=30
# AVALORIA_INBOX_RATE_WINDOW_MS=60000

# Optional. The audio upload's own bucket, deliberately tighter than the text inbox's
# above. The scarce resource on this route is bytes, not requests: 30 uploads a minute at
# the 8 MiB ceiling is 240 MiB per caller per minute of buffering and disk, where 30 text
# submissions are at most half a megabyte.
# AVALORIA_AUDIO_RATE_LIMIT=10
# AVALORIA_AUDIO_RATE_WINDOW_MS=60000

# Optional. The admin read's own bucket, separate from the child write path's so busy
# submitting cannot exhaust the admin view's allowance or the other way round.
# AVALORIA_ADMIN_RATE_LIMIT=60
# AVALORIA_ADMIN_RATE_WINDOW_MS=60000

# Optional. The admin sign-in's own buckets, separate from the family sign-in's. The
# global one is the ceiling a spoofed x-forwarded-for cannot reset, and it is lower than
# the family equivalent because far fewer people hold this code.
# AVALORIA_ADMIN_SESSION_RATE_LIMIT=20
# AVALORIA_ADMIN_SESSION_RATE_WINDOW_MS=60000
# AVALORIA_ADMIN_SESSION_GLOBAL_RATE_LIMIT=30
# AVALORIA_ADMIN_SESSION_GLOBAL_RATE_WINDOW_MS=60000

# Optional. Ceiling on sign-in attempts for the whole process, whatever caller address
# each attempt claims. This is the one a spoofed x-forwarded-for cannot reset.
# AVALORIA_SESSION_GLOBAL_RATE_LIMIT=60
# AVALORIA_SESSION_GLOBAL_RATE_WINDOW_MS=60000
